Subject: [PATCH] vscode: the Custom Endpoint group asks the gateway's
 Responses API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed: magpie wrote VS Code's Custom Endpoint group for the
gateway's Chat Completions (apiType "chat-completions", each model at
/v1/chat/completions, reasoningEffortFormat "chat-completions"). VS
Code's chat-completions client takes a thinking part's id from GitHub
CAPI's own fields alone (#5907, Lynn-zy), so the gateway's standard
reasoning_content deltas reached its renderer without ids — and its
renderer, finding the id empty, renamed it a timestamp a frame and split
on the mismatch, chopping a full chain of thought into a bullet a frame.
The group is written for the Responses API now (apiType "responses",
each model at /v1/responses, reasoningEffortFormat "responses" beside
supportsReasoningEffort), whose thinking deltas name a stable item_id;
the reporter moved the three fields by hand and the chopping went away.
The OpenAI Compatible provider (VSCodium's) and the JetBrains plugin go
on asking Chat Completions, and Check reads the url the group was
written for.

Run: on the commit before, TestVSCode and
TestVSCodeCustomEndpointAsksResponses (new) fail — apiType
"chat-completions", url /v1/chat/completions, reasoningEffortFormat
"chat-completions" (absent on a model without efforts); with the change
all three read responses, the customoai group still reads
chat-completions with no apiType, and TestVSCodeRoundTrip,
TestVSCodeProfiles, TestVSCodeInsiders, TestVSCodeUA, TestVSCodium,
TestVSCodiumCopilotChatOpenAICompatible,
TestVSCodiumModelsUseTheirOwnVisibility and
TestAgentsTakeTheUsersMaxOutput stay green. go test -tags nogui
-count=1 ./internal/agent/ on those; gofmt clean; go vet -tags nogui
./internal/agent/ clean.

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
